Line 1: "plus" can't be part of a name, because it already means something in EasyScript.
    let price plus tax be 5
              ^^^^
Try a name without it, like "price tax".

Line 2: "of" can't be part of a name, because it already means something in EasyScript.
    let rate of pay be 1
             ^^
Try a name without it, like "pay rate".

Line 3: "is" can't be part of a name, because it already means something in EasyScript.
    keep top is big as 3
             ^^
Try a name without it, like "top big".

Line 4: "and" can't be part of a name, because it already means something in EasyScript.
    add 5 to price and tax
                   ^^^
Try a name without it, like "price tax".

Line 5: "and" can't be part of a name, because it already means something in EasyScript.
    to add tax and fees to amount:
               ^^^
Try a name without it, like "add tax fees".

Line 8: I don't understand "fees" here.
    say late fees
             ^^^^
Did you mean "late fee"?

Line 9: A kind in parentheses goes after an input, and inputs come after "with".
    to greet who (text):
                 ^
Write it like "to greet with who (text):".
